    <briefdescription>
<para>Non-blocking operation would block error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1IOWouldBlockError" kindref="compound">IOWouldBlockError</ref> represents an error when a non-blocking I/O operation would block (EWOULDBLOCK/EAGAIN).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOWouldBlockError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Operation<sp/>would<sp/>block&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>IOWouldBlockError(&quot;Socket<sp/>read<sp/>would<sp/>block<sp/>in<sp/>non-blocking<sp/>mode&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
